        tabLabel: 'About',
        pages: [
          {
            title: 'Taroky Nebraska',
            subtitle: 'Card Game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Nebraska Taroky is a four-player trick-taking game played mainly by people of Czech descent in Nebraska. 54-card Tarok pack: 22 trumps (Skies/Å kÃ½z highest, then 21 down to 1) and four suits of 8. Play is clockwise (unlike European Taroky). Bidder chooses partner by calling a King (not trump XIX). Object: win tricks with valuable cards. Follow suit; trump if void. Count cards in packets of three, subtract 2 per packet. Bonuses for declared combinations. Typically played for money with settlements after each hand.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Country/Region of Origin: USA (Nebraska), Czech Republic (Bohemian roots). Rules based on variants played around 1900 in the Bohemian Crown (Habsburg Empire). Preserved by Czech-American communities in the American Midwest.',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Four active players. A fifth may take part as non-playing dealer who deals to the other four and does not take part in play or scoring for that deal. Play is clockwise, unlike European Taroky.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '54-card Tarok pack (22 trumps + 8 per suit)',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '54-card Tarock pack, score sheet',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '12 cards each, 6 in Blind; clockwise',
              },
            ],
          },
        ],
      },
